          "description": "PURPOSE: Read an unsigned 8-bit byte from emulated memory at the given system bus address. USAGE: Use for single-byte status flags, counters, and 8-bit fields. For 16- or 32-bit values use mgba_read16/read32 (one call instead of multi-byte assembly); for spans of more than ~4 bytes use mgba_read_range (one round-trip instead of N frame-latency hops). Reads work the same way whether emulation is paused or running, so pause is optional but recommended when you need a coherent snapshot across multiple reads. BEHAVIOR: No side effects — pure read. Returns an error if the address is outside the platform",
